notes.body:
Please note that:

- [wiretap/blf.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/wiretap/blf.c?ref_type=heads) reads files in Vector Informatik's BLF format and provides CAN frames from them to Wireshark/TShark/etc. as SocketCAN frames;
- [wiretap/busmaster.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/wiretap/busmaster.c?ref_type=heads) reads files from [BUSMASTER](http://rbei-etas.github.io/busmaster/) and provides CAN frames from them to Wireshark/TShark/etc. as SocketCAN frames;
- [wiretap/cllog.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/wiretap/cllog.c?ref_type=heads) reads files from CLX000 CAN loggers from CSS Electronics (https://canlogger.csselectronics.com/clx000-docs/cl1000/log/index.html, https://canlogger.csselectronics.com/clx000-docs/cl2000/log/index.html) and provides CAN frames from them to Wireshark/TShark/etc. as SocketCAN frames;

and that Wireshark is therefore capable of writing frame of those types to pcap files with a link-layer type of `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN` and pcapng files with interfaces with a link-layer type of `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN`; unless those file types guarantee that all CAN CC frames have 8 octets of data and all CAN FD frames have 64 octets of data, then checking, in `LINKTYPE_CAN_SOCKETCAN` files, for a total packet size (including the header) of 16 octets as a CAN CC indicator and a total packet size (including the header) of 72 octets as a CAN FD indicator, without also checking `CANFD_FDF`, is not guaranteed to work.

